    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0560" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/17408</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Collector Cobb to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-10T20:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1916, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Indications are that Carranza authorities will resent American troops entering
                    Mexico. They are rushing troops to Juarez as, I think, predicate to claiming
                    ours unnecessary. Ours are necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
